gay|same-gender-attraction|ADJECTIVE|attracted to people of the same gender|Romantically or sexually attracted to people of the same gender.|đồng tính|The film follows a gay couple restoring a village cinema.|Bộ phim kể về một cặp đôi đồng tính đang phục hồi một rạp chiếu phim trong làng.|Used before a noun or after a linking verb; gay people uses it as an adjective. The older cheerful sense depends on historical context.|0
injury|physical-harm|NOUN|harm to a person's body|Damage or harm to a person's body.|chấn thương; vết thương|An ankle injury kept the dancer out of the final performance.|Một chấn thương ở cổ chân khiến vũ công không tham gia buổi diễn cuối cùng.|Countable for a particular injury, uncountable for harm in general; an injury to a body part identifies the location.|0
penalty|punishment|NOUN|punishment for breaking a rule|A punishment or disadvantage imposed for breaking a law, rule, or agreement.|hình phạt; khoản phạt|The competition imposed a penalty for submitting an entry after the deadline.|Cuộc thi áp dụng hình phạt đối với việc nộp bài dự thi quá hạn.|Countable; a penalty for an action or impose a penalty on someone. The word does not specify the amount or form of punishment.|0
penalty|football-kick|NOUN|kick awarded for an infringement|In football, a kick at goal awarded for certain infringements of the rules.|quả phạt đền|The goalkeeper saved the penalty near the end of the match.|Thủ môn cản được quả phạt đền gần cuối trận đấu.|Countable; take, score, miss, or save a penalty. Penalty kick is the fuller expression; the sporting context supplies the rules.|1
severe|very-serious|ADJECTIVE|very serious or harsh|Very serious, strong, or harsh in its effects.|nghiêm trọng; dữ dội; khắc nghiệt|The village faced severe water shortages during the dry season.|Ngôi làng đối mặt với tình trạng thiếu nước nghiêm trọng trong mùa khô.|Used with damage, shortage, weather, or punishment; severity is the related noun. Severe does not necessarily mean physically large.|0
weed|unwanted-plant|NOUN|plant growing where it is unwanted|A plant growing in a place where it is not wanted.|cỏ dại; cây mọc không mong muốn|A weed had pushed through a crack beside the garden gate.|Một cây cỏ dại mọc xuyên qua khe nứt bên cạnh cổng vườn.|Countable; a weed in a garden or weeds among crops. The label depends on location and purpose rather than a fixed botanical species.|0
